{
  "_readme": [
    "Moxie's safety rules — the whole table, in one file a parent can read.",
    "",
    "This file IS the v1 classifier: moxie_sdk/safety.py only compiles and applies it.",
    "Nothing is hidden in code, nothing is sent to a cloud service, and you can edit this",
    "file (or point MOXIE_SAFETY_RULES at your own copy) to change what Moxie checks.",
    "",
    "WARNING: to filter offensive words a filter has to list them. The `words` arrays",
    "below contain slurs and profanity on purpose. That is the only reason they are here.",
    "",
    "Each category has:",
    "  id          - the string that appears in InputSafety.blocked_by on the wire",
    "  label       - what the parent console calls it",
    "  action      - what happens, per side: 'block' (never spoken, redirect instead),",
    "                'flag' (allowed through, recorded for a parent to review), 'allow'",
    "                'child' = something the child said; 'moxie' = something Moxie is about to say",
    "  escalate    - true for the categories a parent should look at first",
    "  intents     - InputSafety.intents on the wire",
    "  phrase_set  - which redirect line Moxie speaks when this category blocks",
    "  words       - matched whole-word only (\\b...\\b), case/accent/leet-insensitive",
    "  phrases     - regular expressions, matched on the same normalized text",
    "  allow       - false-positive guards: these spans are REMOVED before this category",
    "                is matched, so 'shoot a photo' never counts as violence",
    "  allow_moxie - guards applied on Moxie's side ONLY: a refusal that quotes the request",
    "                ('I can't tell you how to make a sword'), a warning ('never drink",
    "                bleach'), an idiom ('blow up the balloons') or a story character ('the",
    "                bear hurt himself when he fell'). Never on the child's side, where such",
    "                a guard would let a second, harmful clause through ('my grades fell and",
    "                now i want to hurt myself'). The content brain's memory filter judges a",
    "                fact about the child on her side WITHOUT these (safety.py `her_guards`).",
    "  phrases_moxie - phrases matched on Moxie's side ONLY: words a child may say but she",
    "                never does ('don't tell a grown-up', 'our little secret').",
    "",
    "Order matters: the first blocking category in this list picks the spoken redirect."
  ],
